---
/* THE LANDING IS THE LESSON.
 *
 * A stranger cannot try this product — access is invite-gated — and its value,
 * verified work rather than video, is invisible from outside. Every competitor
 * in the category claims an AI tutor, so a claim buys nothing here. This page
 * does not describe the loop: it runs one real lesson, takes one real answer,
 * and returns one real verdict from the same evaluator a logged-in learner
 * gets, before asking for anything. The wall arrives after the value.
 *
 * The lesson itself is now in the HTML — title, video plate, written guide, key
 * points, and the question. It used to arrive after a fetch, which is why the
 * page visibly assembled itself in front of the reader.
 */
import Public from '../layouts/Public.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import TutorPanel from '../components/TutorPanel.astro';
import FounderNote from '../components/FounderNote.astro';
import Doors from '../components/Doors.astro';
import DemoAsk from '../components/DemoAsk.svelte';
import VideoPlate from '../components/VideoPlate.svelte';
import GuideToggle from '../components/GuideToggle.svelte';
import { SITE_NAME, TUTOR, STEPS, GETS } from '../lib/site.js';
import { renderMarkdown, assertNoMermaid } from '../lib/markdown.js';
import lesson from '../data/demo.json';

const guideSource = lesson.written || lesson.transcript || '';
assertNoMermaid(guideSource, 'the landing demo lesson');
const guideHtml = renderMarkdown(guideSource);

/* What the island actually needs, and nothing else.
   Astro serializes an island's props into the HTML so it can hydrate with the
   same values the build used. Handing it the whole lesson therefore shipped the
   written guide, the transcript and the key points a SECOND time inside an
   attribute — 5.8KB of a 28KB page, none of it read. */
const ask = {
  explain_prompt: lesson.explain_prompt,
  doc_type: lesson.doc_type,
  exercise: lesson.exercise?.instruction ? { instruction: lesson.exercise.instruction } : null,
  reto: lesson.reto?.scenario ? { scenario: lesson.reto.scenario } : null,
};
---
<Public
  here="clase"
  title={`${SITE_NAME} — aprende haciendo, con tutora IA`}
  description="Haz una clase real ahora mismo, sin cuenta: mira el video, lee la guía y explícalo con tus palabras. Tu tutora te responde de verdad."
>
  {/* The first viewport issues an imperative — "haz una clase" — and used to
      offer no way to obey it: the box was 2,837px down, 3.4 phone screens for a
      reader who studies in stolen time. The hero carries the question itself,
      so the page's verb and the page's affordance agree. */}
  <section class="u-full band-hi hero">
    <div class="u-wide herogrid">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">Una clase de verdad, ahora, sin cuenta</div>
        <h1>No te contamos cómo funciona. Haz una clase.</h1>
        <p class="muted lede">
          Primera lección del curso de {lesson.course_title}, entera. Explícala
          con tus palabras y {TUTOR} te contesta de verdad — antes de pedirte
          nada, y sin cuenta.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div><DemoAsk lesson={ask} client:load /></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="lessonsplit u-wide" style="margin-top:var(--s4)">
    <div>
      <div class="microlabel">{lesson.course_title} · lección 1</div>
      <h2 class="lessontitle" style="margin:6px 0 10px">{lesson.title}</h2>
      {lesson.has_video && <VideoPlate client:visible />}
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="ai-tag" style="margin-bottom:8px"><span class="dot"></span> La guía escrita</div>
      {/* The guide is rendered at build time with raw HTML escaped, which is
          a stronger control than the runtime sanitiser it replaces — see
          lib/markdown.js. It is slotted into the island, so it ships in the
          HTML once and is never serialized into the island's props. */}
      <GuideToggle client:visible>
        <div class="guidewrap card card-paper written" set:html={guideHtml}></div>
      </GuideToggle>
    </div>
  </div>

  {/* Key points sit BELOW the split, not in the left column. The guide starts
      collapsed, so the right column is shorter than the video column and this
      card used to leave a large dead field beside it on a wide screen. */}
  {lesson.key_points?.length > 0 && (
    <div class="card keypoints u-wide" style="margin-top:var(--s4)">
      <div class="microlabel">Lo que te llevas</div>
      <div class="kpgrid" style="margin-top:var(--s2)">
        {lesson.key_points.map((p) => (
          <div class="gaprow">
            <span class="gx" style="color:var(--amber)"><Icon name="check" class="ic ic-s" /></span>
            <span>{p}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  )}

  {/* One worked example, after the lesson, never beside the box. There used to
      be two — the same component with the same caption 2,800px apart, which read
      as a repeat. And on a phone the first thing under the headline was a
      stranger's answer: a product that promises to read YOUR work opening with
      someone else's, in the exact anatomy of a testimonial, on a site that has
      correctly refused to have testimonials.
      Deliberately still a WRONG answer, and the one carrying a misconception —
      that is the mechanic nothing else in the category has. */}
  <div class="u-wide afterq">
    <TutorPanel key="todavia" class="tp-inline" />
    <div class="afterq-note">
      <p class="muted t-sm">
        Esto es lo que recibe cualquiera que escriba algo arriba: un veredicto,
        el error de fondo si lo hay, y qué le falta — no una nota.
        La misma {TUTOR} que lee el trabajo de quienes ya están dentro.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  {/* Cómo funciona, on two axes, because those are the two questions a stranger
      actually has: QUÉ HAGO (numbered steps, in order) and QUÉ RECIBO. */}
  <section class="u-full band-lo">
    <div class="microlabel">Cómo funciona · cuatro pasos</div>
    <div class="u-wide steps" style="margin-top:var(--s4)">
      {STEPS.map(([title, text], i) => (
        <div class="card">
          <div class="stephead">
            <span class="stepnum">{i + 1}</span>
            <b class="t-md">{title}</b>
          </div>
          <p class="muted t-sm" style="margin-top:8px">{text}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="u-wide" style="margin-top:var(--s6)">
    <div class="microlabel">Qué te llevas</div>
    <div class="takeaways" style="margin-top:var(--s4)">
      {GETS.map(([ic, title, text]) => (
        <div class="card">
          <div class="row" style="gap:10px;color:var(--amber)">
            <Icon name={ic} />
            <b class="t-md" style="color:var(--text)">{title}</b>
          </div>
          <p class="muted t-sm" style="margin-top:8px">{text}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="faint t-sm" style="margin:var(--s4) 2px 0">
      No damos certificados: nadie contrata por uno nuestro. Damos el trabajo que
      hiciste, con tu nombre.
    </p>
  </section>

  {/* El umbral, and it comes BEFORE the library on purpose. The peak of this
      page is a machine quoting a stranger's own words back at them. That peak
      used to be followed by an explainer and a course grid, so the last thing
      read before the decision was an inventory — which is mechanically why the
      best demo in the category was remembered as a marketplace. */}
  <section class="u-full band-deep threshold">
    <div>
      <div class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--amber)">Fase alfa</div>
      <h2 style="margin-top:var(--s3)">Ahora la parte que no se ve desde afuera.</h2>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:var(--s4)">
        Eso fue una lección. Lo que de verdad hace el sistema es lo otro: dinos
        qué quieres ser y te armamos la ruta — qué módulos, en qué orden — y te
        decimos con nombre y apellido <b>lo que ese puesto pide y nosotros no
        enseñamos</b>. Casi nadie te dice eso.
      </p>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:var(--s4)">
        Cada persona que entra escribe trabajo real y {TUTOR} lo lee de verdad.
        Eso no escala de golpe, así que abrimos por invitación y de a pocos.
      </p>
    </div>
    <FounderNote />
    <Doors kind="lit" />
  </section>

  {/* The library, as inventory and nothing more: one sentence and a quiet link,
      AFTER the decision. It used to be a first-class section whose fourteen
      course names were fourteen of the page's seventeen h3s — so the document
      outline of this homepage literally was a course catalog. */}
  <p class="muted t-sm center" style="margin:var(--s6) 0 var(--s2)">
    Detrás de esto hay <b>70 módulos</b> en 14 cursos. Tu ruta los ordena según
    lo que tu puesto pide, no según el índice de un curso.
    <a class="doorlink" href="/cursos">Ver qué enseñamos</a>
  </p>
</Public>
